AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, and Kotlin
-------------------------------------
Pocket Numbat uses AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, the Kotlin standard library,
and Kotlin coroutines. These components are licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. See LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

European Central Bank exchange rates
------------------------------------
The app downloads the ECB euro foreign exchange reference rates from
https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/eurofxref/eurofxref-daily.xml and passes them
unchanged to the Numbat engine. The ECB publishes these rates for reuse with
attribution. The rates are cached on the device for offline use.

